WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.020 --> 00:01.030
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.060 --> 00:02.310
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:02.330 --> 00:05.010
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:25.020 --> 00:26.440
Can I go with you?

6
00:28.400 --> 00:29.820
I forgot to bring my umbrella.

7
00:30.670 --> 00:32.200
If I say you can't,

8
00:32.730 --> 00:34.000
will you go away?

9
00:48.980 --> 00:50.100
Why are you teasing me like that?

10
00:51.400 --> 00:52.520
I'm just kidding.

11
00:56.130 --> 00:57.400
I want you to know

12
00:58.010 --> 00:59.790
that I didn't want you to go far away.

13
01:10.410 --> 01:11.410
At last,

14
01:12.500 --> 01:15.290
I finally get to see the girl under the yellow umbrella

15
01:15.310 --> 01:17.300
I've always dreamt of.

16
01:25.240 --> 01:28.810
[North Star Entertainment]

17
01:30.700 --> 01:32.700
[Presents]

18
01:33.540 --> 01:36.600
[Third Person]

19
01:38.800 --> 01:48.130
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

20
01:48.680 --> 01:53.810
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

21
01:53.840 --> 01:57.450
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

22
01:58.180 --> 02:03.870
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

23
02:03.890 --> 02:13.320
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

24
02:13.720 --> 02:18.770
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

25
02:18.790 --> 02:23.070
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

26
02:23.090 --> 02:32.010
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

27
02:32.480 --> 02:40.610
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

28
03:51.970 --> 03:53.200
Can I go with you?

29
03:53.600 --> 03:55.110
I forgot to bring my umbrella.

30
04:02.130 --> 04:03.020
Thank you

31
04:03.180 --> 04:04.400
for letting me go with you.

32
04:35.600 --> 04:38.490
Ever since I lost my memories four years ago,

33
04:39.250 --> 04:41.690
I've dreamt of the time I fell in love.

34
04:43.200 --> 04:46.490
I don't know if it's a memory or just my imagination.

35
04:47.150 --> 04:48.820
But the dream world

36
04:49.290 --> 04:51.110
is more interesting than reality.

37
05:04.610 --> 05:05.610
Kiiro,

38
05:06.300 --> 05:07.300
aren't you bored

39
05:08.010 --> 05:10.300
of eating the same food

40
05:10.630 --> 05:11.990
and staying in the same place every day?

41
05:18.180 --> 05:19.180
What am I even asking?

42
05:20.060 --> 05:21.720
What choice do you have?

43
05:25.800 --> 05:26.800
But it's alright,

44
05:26.900 --> 05:28.900
you aren't stuck here alone.

45
05:31.020 --> 05:32.020
I'm stuck here too.

46
05:40.580 --> 05:41.410
Whatever.

47
05:41.990 --> 05:43.400
We don't have a choice anyway.

48
06:02.250 --> 06:04.610
Others might run to exercise,

49
06:04.630 --> 06:06.170
to focus,

50
06:06.190 --> 06:07.680
or to compete.

51
06:07.700 --> 06:10.240
But I run because I don't know what else to do.

52
06:10.260 --> 06:12.160
I run to pass the time

53
06:12.490 --> 06:14.200
so that I can go back to sleep and dream.

54
07:00.270 --> 07:01.470
I never thought...

55
07:01.490 --> 07:03.600
my dream would be right in front of me.

56
07:16.220 --> 07:17.120
Is that all?

57
07:17.820 --> 07:19.210
Are there any apples missing?

58
07:20.880 --> 07:22.490
Better not go missing again.

59
07:27.870 --> 07:28.690
I mean...

60
07:28.900 --> 07:29.900
the apples.

61
07:32.790 --> 07:34.720
Without your help,

62
07:34.980 --> 07:36.410
it might've been a lot harder for me.

63
07:37.310 --> 07:38.810
Thank you so much.

64
07:39.600 --> 07:40.600
It's alright.

65
07:40.830 --> 07:41.790
No trouble at all.

66
07:45.040 --> 07:46.600
Let me help you, too.

67
07:54.230 --> 07:55.230
Then...

68
07:57.570 --> 07:58.910
Can I go with you?

69
08:04.330 --> 08:05.330
Of course,

70
08:05.350 --> 08:06.890
wherever you're going,

71
08:07.110 --> 08:08.400
I'll take you there.

72
08:15.660 --> 08:17.600
I also don't want you to get wet.

73
08:19.540 --> 08:21.090
Then...

74
08:30.800 --> 08:31.900
Why is...

75
08:32.690 --> 08:36.280
the world suddenly less dull?

76
08:40.640 --> 08:42.400
I think the rain has stopped.

77
08:48.110 --> 08:48.940
Thank you

78
08:48.960 --> 08:50.400
for walking with me this far.

79
08:52.620 --> 08:54.410
Please... excuse me.

80
08:57.530 --> 08:58.490
Here.

81
09:08.870 --> 09:09.400
Oh!

82
09:19.200 --> 09:20.390
Are you alright?

83
09:22.690 --> 09:24.110
I should be asking you that.

84
09:32.960 --> 09:34.810
[Emergency Room]

85
09:37.260 --> 09:39.560
Please collect your medicine that way.

86
09:39.580 --> 09:40.690
- Thank you. - Yes.

87
09:45.760 --> 09:48.100
She's the owner of that flowerpot.

88
09:49.020 --> 09:49.510
Well...

89
09:49.690 --> 09:50.790
you seem fine now.

90
09:51.270 --> 09:52.390
I'll leave then.

91
09:52.510 --> 09:54.000
What a waste of time.

92
09:54.150 --> 09:55.300
Hey,

93
09:55.430 --> 09:57.640
aren't you going to take responsibility for hurting her?

94
09:57.710 --> 09:59.240
And who told you to walk around there?

95
09:59.910 --> 10:01.010
How was I supposed to know

96
10:01.140 --> 10:03.000
someone would be walking by?

97
10:03.310 --> 10:05.610
And you think it's okay to throw a flowerpot like that?

98
10:06.240 --> 10:07.520
It's my flowerpot.

99
10:07.620 --> 10:09.020
Whatever I do with it is none of your business!

100
10:09.190 --> 10:10.420
But you threw it at a person!

101
10:10.440 --> 10:11.330
Then why were you walking there?!

102
10:11.350 --> 10:12.420
Please stop.

103
10:13.290 --> 10:14.920
I'm fine...

104
10:16.890 --> 10:17.610
See?

105
10:18.060 --> 10:19.890
She said she's fine.

106
10:20.290 --> 10:21.810
So stop sticking your nose in.

107
10:23.920 --> 10:25.810
I'm really okay now.

108
10:26.750 --> 10:28.210
Let's go to the police station.

109
10:29.060 --> 10:30.420
Let the police handle this.

110
10:37.320 --> 10:39.310
I thought you'd be angrier,

111
10:39.710 --> 10:40.200
but...

112
10:40.220 --> 10:42.920
you asked for the flowerpot that fell on you as compensation?

113
10:43.470 --> 10:45.280
Don't you want compensation for wasting your time?

114
10:47.190 --> 10:48.190
What about you?

115
10:48.640 --> 10:49.510
Hm?

116
10:50.380 --> 10:52.400
You're the one whose time was wasted

117
10:52.490 --> 10:53.710
because you helped me.

118
10:55.510 --> 10:57.510
You are the one helping me.

119
10:57.620 --> 10:58.710
Without you,

120
10:58.830 --> 11:00.310
I would've gotten injured.

121
11:01.190 --> 11:02.310
Then that's alright.

122
11:04.640 --> 11:06.400
We helped each other out.

123
11:08.940 --> 11:10.720
And this plant, too.

124
11:11.840 --> 11:13.590
It's not even dead yet.

125
11:13.910 --> 11:15.190
But she threw it away?

126
11:16.840 --> 11:19.010
From the looks of it, it might not survive.

127
11:19.590 --> 11:21.390
I don't even know what plant this is.

128
11:22.990 --> 11:24.410
It's a rose plant.

129
11:24.800 --> 11:26.270
If it survives...

130
11:26.550 --> 11:28.790
The flowers would be beautiful.

131
11:32.520 --> 11:35.000
You want roses that much?

132
11:38.450 --> 11:39.900
I want another chance.

133
11:44.570 --> 11:46.300
Everyone who has made mistakes

134
11:46.560 --> 11:47.990
would probably want another chance.

135
11:48.480 --> 11:50.500
If they're sorry

136
11:51.210 --> 11:52.390
and have already apologized,

137
11:53.880 --> 11:56.000
I'm willing to forgive them.

138
11:58.780 --> 12:00.110
How kind of you.

139
12:01.790 --> 12:02.790
Not really.

140
12:05.270 --> 12:07.320
I wanted another chance as well.

141
12:10.060 --> 12:11.300
Both me...

142
12:12.880 --> 12:13.880
and the rose.

143
12:17.930 --> 12:19.110
How sad...

144
12:20.040 --> 12:22.090
I couldn't understand anything you said.

145
12:23.870 --> 12:25.800
Then would you like to listen a little longer?

146
12:28.490 --> 12:30.590
My condo isn't far from here,

147
12:31.280 --> 12:33.590
so can you bring this rose plant...

148
12:34.160 --> 12:35.900
to its home?

149
12:55.980 --> 12:57.590
You're... all wet.

150
12:57.610 --> 12:59.920
Would you like to come inside to shower and change?

151
13:01.920 --> 13:02.910
Normally...

152
13:02.990 --> 13:06.170
do people go into a stranger's room after meeting them only once?

153
13:09.650 --> 13:10.800
You're right...

154
13:14.410 --> 13:15.410
I'm Chris.

155
13:16.420 --> 13:17.520
What's your name?

156
13:18.010 --> 13:19.120
I'm Sun.

157
13:31.240 --> 13:33.000
Nice to meet you, Sun.

158
13:34.050 --> 13:35.190
I'll be in your care.

159
13:36.100 --> 13:38.000
Nice to meet you, too.

160
13:38.940 --> 13:39.720
Chris...

161
13:58.320 --> 14:00.090
Feel free to use the bathroom.

162
14:00.140 --> 14:01.300
Wash your hair, too.

163
14:01.500 --> 14:03.210
Bangkok is full of pollution and dust.

164
14:05.580 --> 14:06.580
Okay.

165
15:33.720 --> 15:34.790
Here's some hot cocoa.

166
15:34.890 --> 15:36.110
It'll help warm you up.

167
15:37.710 --> 15:38.700
Thank you.

168
15:39.710 --> 15:41.810
But this is Thailand.

169
15:41.890 --> 15:44.470
It'll only be cold for a few days before it gets hot again.

170
15:45.710 --> 15:46.490
But...

171
15:47.200 --> 15:48.610
you're shivering.

172
15:49.940 --> 15:51.900
I'd better drink something warm.

173
16:00.720 --> 16:02.880
I've never had cocoa like this before.

174
16:02.900 --> 16:03.900
How did you make this?

175
16:03.920 --> 16:04.960
It's so delicious.

176
16:05.280 --> 16:06.280
It's my secret recipe.

177
16:06.590 --> 16:07.890
If you want to have this,

178
16:08.820 --> 16:10.430
you can only get it here.

179
16:20.820 --> 16:22.600
I like your shampoo.

180
16:22.750 --> 16:24.200
It smells so good.

181
16:38.700 --> 16:39.900
It actually is.

182
16:40.690 --> 16:43.080
I like this smell when it's on you, too.

183
17:11.480 --> 17:12.830
[Nadear]

184
17:14.290 --> 17:15.210
Ow...

185
17:16.080 --> 17:16.920
Sun...

186
17:17.110 --> 17:18.880
I'm sorry. Are you hurt?

187
17:19.000 --> 17:20.000
Let me see.

188
17:20.720 --> 17:21.530
Whoa.

189
17:21.630 --> 17:22.730
Does it hurt?

190
17:27.220 --> 17:28.610
I forgive you.

191
17:29.600 --> 17:30.690
It's okay.

192
17:41.960 --> 17:43.560
[Nadear]

193
17:47.840 --> 17:49.200
Don't you need to head back now?

194
17:49.820 --> 17:51.100
They're calling you.

195
17:55.300 --> 17:56.220
Chris,

196
17:58.300 --> 18:00.510
can I ask you something personal?

197
18:03.240 --> 18:04.360
What is it?

198
18:05.740 --> 18:07.310
Do you have a partner?

199
18:10.200 --> 18:12.070
I... don't have a partner.

200
18:38.050 --> 18:41.880
[Third Person]

201
18:43.008 --> 18:46.988
[Third Person]

202
19:33.698 --> 19:34.788
Chris.

203
19:35.798 --> 19:36.598
Chris.

204
19:37.678 --> 19:38.468
Chris?

205
19:40.188 --> 19:41.098
Chris?

206
19:44.338 --> 19:46.788
You went quiet after I said I don't have a partner.

207
19:47.188 --> 19:48.298
What were you thinking about?

208
19:50.328 --> 19:52.568
Uh, it's nothing.

209
19:55.018 --> 19:56.398
Thinking of something lewd, aren't you?

210
19:57.068 --> 19:58.398
No!

211
19:59.598 --> 20:01.688
I really wasn't thinking about anything like that.

212
20:03.578 --> 20:06.058
But your reaction tells me otherwise.

213
20:07.098 --> 20:07.808
Well,

214
20:09.598 --> 20:10.598
what were you thinking about?

215
20:12.088 --> 20:13.188
I want to know your lewd thoughts.

216
20:27.888 --> 20:28.988
I forgot.

217
20:29.608 --> 20:30.798
I have a meeting today.

218
20:35.138 --> 20:35.938
Then...

219
20:35.958 --> 20:37.198
I won't trouble you any longer.

220
20:37.218 --> 20:37.998
I'll take my leave.

221
20:38.018 --> 20:39.398
The rain has stopped as well.

222
20:42.978 --> 20:43.778
Does that mean...

223
20:43.998 --> 20:45.488
if I don't have work

224
20:45.638 --> 20:47.078
and it's still raining,

225
20:47.738 --> 20:49.298
you're not going to leave?

226
20:50.848 --> 20:51.698
Yes?

227
20:53.658 --> 20:54.688
Just kidding.

228
20:55.768 --> 20:57.108
But this is the first time

229
20:57.708 --> 20:59.398
I want to skip my meeting,

230
20:59.818 --> 21:00.678
and...

231
21:01.358 --> 21:03.178
want it to rain all day.

232
21:18.618 --> 21:19.608
Take this with you

233
21:19.628 --> 21:20.678
in case it rains again.

234
21:22.498 --> 21:23.488
Thank you.

235
21:29.198 --> 21:29.988
Um...

236
21:30.008 --> 21:31.008
Sun.

237
21:31.988 --> 21:32.698
Yes?

238
21:34.588 --> 21:36.168
Thank you for today.

239
21:41.048 --> 21:41.838
Then...

240
21:41.958 --> 21:43.088
please excuse me.

241
21:46.718 --> 21:48.198
Will you come running again tomorrow?

242
21:51.918 --> 21:53.878
I usually run every day.

243
21:54.868 --> 21:55.588
That's great.

244
21:55.608 --> 21:56.978
I want to run tomorrow as well.

245
22:15.798 --> 22:17.198
Hello, Kiiro.

246
22:18.038 --> 22:19.478
You'd definitely be jealous of me

247
22:19.498 --> 22:21.198
if you knew what happened today.

248
22:23.168 --> 22:24.498
You're back, Chris?

249
22:26.808 --> 22:28.088
I called you several times.

250
22:28.108 --> 22:29.658
Why didn't you answer?

251
22:32.108 --> 22:33.908
I haven't made a reservation yet.

252
22:37.288 --> 22:38.488
Where do you think...

253
22:39.318 --> 22:42.338
we should go celebrate our tenth anniversary?

254
22:47.238 --> 22:49.098
Do you have a place you want to go?

255
22:49.878 --> 22:51.208
I'm fine with anywhere.

256
22:53.318 --> 22:54.698
Pick wherever you like.

257
22:57.988 --> 22:59.248
You know

258
22:59.278 --> 23:01.688
there's only one place I like.

259
23:04.978 --> 23:06.058
Our place.

260
23:13.028 --> 23:14.758
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

261
23:14.778 --> 23:15.448
Oh, Chris,

262
23:15.648 --> 23:16.748
long time no see.

263
23:16.768 --> 23:17.598
Doing well?

264
23:18.208 --> 23:18.988
Yeah, Nan.

265
23:19.088 --> 23:20.378
I'm fine, as usual.

266
23:20.428 --> 23:21.988
Nadear took good care of you, huh?

267
23:22.088 --> 23:24.298
She just asked me to reserve a table.

268
23:24.828 --> 23:25.688
But seriously,

269
23:25.708 --> 23:27.708
don't you guys ever eat anywhere else?

270
23:28.568 --> 23:31.108
If we eat here, all three of us make money.

271
23:31.318 --> 23:32.118
Isn't that good?

272
23:33.278 --> 23:34.728
Or you don't want it?

273
23:34.878 --> 23:36.028
Want to pull out your shares, then?

274
23:36.308 --> 23:37.678
I'm just teasing you.

275
23:38.068 --> 23:39.638
You only have to say the word,

276
23:39.658 --> 23:41.468
and I'll reserve a VIP table

277
23:41.488 --> 23:43.048
with a special menu

278
23:43.068 --> 23:45.678
for my shareholders, sisters, and family.

279
23:46.158 --> 23:47.778
Alright, I'll lead the way.

280
23:49.688 --> 23:50.388
Nadear...

281
23:51.778 --> 23:53.288
Are your parents here yet?

282
23:54.298 --> 23:56.078
If I tell you they're already here,

283
23:56.188 --> 23:58.488
will you stop frowning?

284
24:14.048 --> 24:15.278
Congratulations, dear.

285
24:15.468 --> 24:17.298
Time really flies, huh?

286
24:17.598 --> 24:18.828
Before we know it,

287
24:19.088 --> 24:21.298
you two have been dating for a decade.

288
24:22.458 --> 24:23.578
Look at your mother and me.

289
24:24.058 --> 24:25.578
We've been together for thirty years now.

290
24:25.858 --> 24:27.168
And that isn't easy, dear.

291
24:28.588 --> 24:31.568
Then Chris and I will be together for over thirty years.

292
24:32.598 --> 24:33.878
Is that true, Chris?

293
24:39.778 --> 24:41.408
Of course...

294
24:42.658 --> 24:43.968
Hearing you say that,

295
24:43.988 --> 24:45.578
I feel relieved.

296
24:45.868 --> 24:47.598
I have only one daughter

297
24:47.628 --> 24:49.708
who I love and cherish dearly.

298
24:51.528 --> 24:52.788
Your father and I

299
24:52.808 --> 24:54.408
are getting quite old now.

300
24:55.158 --> 24:57.078
If one day we pass away,

301
24:57.508 --> 24:59.918
I'm just scared that Nadear would be all alone.

302
25:01.018 --> 25:02.018
Dearie...

303
25:02.038 --> 25:04.698
why are you saying sad things on her anniversary?

304
25:04.788 --> 25:06.298
Chris already said

305
25:06.358 --> 25:07.998
they'll be together for over thirty years.

306
25:10.288 --> 25:11.778
Thank you so much, Chris,

307
25:11.948 --> 25:13.448
for taking care of Nadear.

308
25:14.278 --> 25:16.348
I know my daughter

309
25:16.368 --> 25:17.388
is very stubborn.

310
25:17.968 --> 25:20.308
But if you're with her,

311
25:20.858 --> 25:22.778
her father and I can rest easy.

312
25:24.248 --> 25:26.478
But I'd be even more at ease

313
25:26.748 --> 25:28.628
if you made it official.

314
25:30.048 --> 25:32.248
You've been dating for ten years now.

315
25:32.548 --> 25:34.148
You live in the same house

316
25:34.488 --> 25:36.488
and work at the same place.

317
25:37.388 --> 25:39.288
When are you going to get married?

318
26:06.788 --> 26:08.718
Nan, the influencer at that table

319
26:08.738 --> 26:09.798
is making a big fuss.

320
26:09.818 --> 26:11.748
She said I gave her the wrong order,

321
26:12.008 --> 26:14.548
but I wrote down exactly what she ordered.

322
26:14.708 --> 26:15.868
Wawah,

323
26:15.888 --> 26:17.158
if I could split myself in two,

324
26:17.178 --> 26:18.198
I'd help you with that.

325
26:18.498 --> 26:19.898
Our head chef is getting complaints

326
26:19.918 --> 26:21.278
because the food hasn't been served yet.

327
26:22.738 --> 26:23.278
Alright,

328
26:23.298 --> 26:24.648
you go calm her down first.

329
26:24.668 --> 26:27.108
I'll go help out in the kitchen, then I'll come help you.

330
26:27.118 --> 26:29.988
If I could do that, why would I come to you in the first place?!

331
26:30.008 --> 26:30.868
Wawah,

332
26:31.418 --> 26:32.768
where is that influencer sitting?

333
26:38.848 --> 26:39.978
Excuse me,

334
26:40.538 --> 26:42.878
my waitress told me you got the wrong order?

335
26:43.128 --> 26:44.938
I ordered baked crab with roe and vermicelli.

336
26:45.078 --> 26:47.148
But I got baked crab and vermicelli.

337
26:47.508 --> 26:48.668
I already ate it,

338
26:48.688 --> 26:50.618
so I knew the crab had no roe in it.

339
26:50.698 --> 26:52.548
I'd like you to remake the dish.

340
26:52.898 --> 26:53.898
Because...

341
26:54.078 --> 26:55.918
I got the wrong dish.

342
26:56.248 --> 26:58.998
But you really ordered baked crab and vermicelli.

343
26:59.358 --> 27:00.538
You didn't say, "Crab with roe."

344
27:01.298 --> 27:03.828
Are you saying I forgot what I said?

345
27:06.298 --> 27:08.498
Then let me offer you a solution.

346
27:08.548 --> 27:10.538
We'll check the security footage.

347
27:10.568 --> 27:12.418
If our waitress is at fault,

348
27:12.588 --> 27:14.688
we'll take full responsibility.

349
27:14.858 --> 27:16.888
So you're going to blame the customer, huh?!

350
27:17.298 --> 27:19.008
You're going to believe her?!

351
27:19.318 --> 27:20.458
I'm your customer!

352
27:22.278 --> 27:24.708
I'm sorry for wasting your time.

353
27:24.868 --> 27:27.688
We'll remake your dish for you.

354
27:28.018 --> 27:29.028
As an apology,

355
27:29.058 --> 27:31.948
we won't charge you for this dish.

356
27:32.838 --> 27:33.898
Excuse me,

357
27:33.938 --> 27:35.378
are you the owner of this restaurant?

358
27:37.188 --> 27:38.188
Yes.

359
27:38.708 --> 27:39.868
No wonder...

360
27:40.688 --> 27:43.138
you handled things better than other employees.

361
27:49.068 --> 27:50.988
Why did you listen to the customer?

362
27:51.298 --> 27:53.068
We didn't even know if it was our fault.

363
27:55.158 --> 27:57.488
I know you want to do what's right,

364
27:58.138 --> 27:59.638
and you don't want to hurt her feelings.

365
28:00.898 --> 28:03.288
But trying to find out the truth is a waste of time.

366
28:03.998 --> 28:06.048
And if the customer is dissatisfied,

367
28:06.138 --> 28:08.808
she might write a bad review, which would make things worse.

368
28:09.968 --> 28:11.668
Even though we're not wrong?

369
28:12.918 --> 28:16.308
Taking the blame is another way to resolve an issue.

370
28:20.058 --> 28:22.828
So you think I can't handle this on my own?

371
28:23.748 --> 28:25.298
This is my restaurant as well.

372
28:25.348 --> 28:27.788
But you haven't worked in a long time.

373
28:28.048 --> 28:29.798
You wouldn't understand the customers.

374
28:31.698 --> 28:32.898
Trust me, alright?

375
28:33.628 --> 28:36.068
Don't let this ruin our special day.

376
28:36.698 --> 28:37.878
Let's go back to lunch.

377
28:38.198 --> 28:39.478
Mom and Dad are waiting.

378
28:43.628 --> 28:44.998
I can only go, can't I?

379
28:48.548 --> 28:50.528
[Happy 10th Anniversary, Chris and Nadear]

380
28:50.548 --> 28:51.638
- Mm, so delicious. - Is it good?

381
28:51.658 --> 28:52.708
There's salted egg.

382
28:53.308 --> 28:54.308
Cholesterol, huh?

383
28:58.158 --> 28:59.478
You won't be lonely anymore.

384
29:00.398 --> 29:01.998
Come live with me, little rose.

385
29:02.228 --> 29:04.288
How did you know it's a rose plant?

386
29:05.098 --> 29:06.098
Have you grown one before?

387
29:06.868 --> 29:08.298
I did when I was younger,

388
29:08.318 --> 29:08.948
but...

389
29:09.548 --> 29:11.188
after I moved, I didn't have any.

390
29:12.878 --> 29:14.598
Do you think it'll survive?

391
29:16.578 --> 29:18.188
It depends on...

392
29:19.758 --> 29:21.388
how you treat it.

393
29:22.888 --> 29:24.498
Treating a plant

394
29:24.678 --> 29:26.218
is like treating a person.

395
29:27.498 --> 29:28.668
If you don't take good care of it,

396
29:29.088 --> 29:30.688
don't water

397
29:31.348 --> 29:32.558
or cherish it,

398
29:34.168 --> 29:35.668
it won't work out.

399
29:40.048 --> 29:42.418
But since this is the rose plant you saved,

400
29:51.548 --> 29:52.718
I'll work it out.

401
29:55.398 --> 29:56.688
Because I want to stay close.

402
30:06.138 --> 30:07.668
The rose plant would be happy to hear that.

403
30:09.098 --> 30:10.568
You're the one who should be happy.

404
30:11.128 --> 30:12.798
The one I want to stay close to

405
30:13.348 --> 30:14.568
is you, Chris.

406
30:51.288 --> 30:52.738
Can't you do this for my parents

407
30:52.758 --> 30:55.188
every once in a while?

408
30:55.498 --> 30:57.198
Why did you have to run away?

409
30:58.138 --> 30:59.898
Did you know I had to lie to them

410
30:59.918 --> 31:02.668
that you were feeling sick, so you couldn't see them off to their car?

411
31:03.828 --> 31:05.988
You're good at lying anyway, aren't you?

412
31:06.778 --> 31:08.478
Just like when you lied to our customer.

413
31:10.288 --> 31:11.808
Is this really your excuse

414
31:11.828 --> 31:13.988
for not seeing my parents off?

415
31:15.388 --> 31:16.388
I'm not making excuses.

416
31:17.848 --> 31:19.808
But you're being sarcastic.

417
31:21.178 --> 31:22.578
That's not okay...

418
31:23.878 --> 31:25.298
Then what can I do?

419
31:25.798 --> 31:26.738
Can I tell you the truth?

420
31:26.758 --> 31:28.308
I don't want to see your parents off

421
31:28.328 --> 31:29.518
because I feel ashamed.

422
31:30.178 --> 31:32.378
I can't face your parents.

423
31:32.838 --> 31:35.058
I can't lie to them any longer.

424
31:36.148 --> 31:36.988
Chris...

425
31:37.358 --> 31:39.008
I can't take this anymore.

426
31:39.398 --> 31:42.468
Pretending we're in love for your parents

427
31:42.798 --> 31:44.488
won't put their minds at ease,

428
31:44.508 --> 31:46.378
so you can live your life freely.

429
31:47.588 --> 31:48.588
Do you know why?

430
31:49.908 --> 31:51.478
Because if we're still together,

431
31:52.538 --> 31:54.068
we'll always fight.

432
31:54.308 --> 31:56.038
Do you have someone else?

433
31:56.778 --> 31:58.298
Why shouldn't I?

434
32:00.778 --> 32:02.278
We broke up a long time ago.

435
32:09.688 --> 32:13.058
[Third Person]

436
32:14.714 --> 32:18.104
[Third Person]

437
32:39.234 --> 32:40.634
I'm sorry...

438
32:41.714 --> 32:43.634
I said mean things to you today.

439
32:46.294 --> 32:47.594
I'll change.

440
32:49.014 --> 32:50.474
It won't happen again.

441
32:56.004 --> 32:57.594
Will you forgive me?

442
32:58.114 --> 32:59.984
Please, Chris...?

443
33:02.854 --> 33:03.893
Okay, okay.

444
33:03.894 --> 33:04.694
Alright.

445
33:06.314 --> 33:08.754
I love you because you're so kind.

446
33:43.524 --> 33:44.854
I'm sorry.

447
33:45.574 --> 33:48.024
I know your body is rejecting this,

448
33:48.994 --> 33:50.694
but I just want to hug you.

449
33:57.514 --> 33:58.834
I'll wait...

450
34:00.174 --> 34:02.674
until you feel better.

451
34:03.484 --> 34:05.494
Until we can hug each other.

452
34:09.604 --> 34:11.334
But it's been four years now, Nadear.

453
34:11.874 --> 34:13.844
No matter how long I have to wait,

454
34:14.234 --> 34:15.784
I won't give up.

455
34:16.604 --> 34:19.474
I'll make you want to hug me.

456
34:22.454 --> 34:24.674
And don't go hugging anyone else before me.

457
34:28.844 --> 34:31.054
But you couldn't do that, could you?

458
34:32.034 --> 34:33.493
You can't even stand

459
34:33.494 --> 34:35.144
touching anyone else.

460
34:37.834 --> 34:39.404
Your past trauma

461
34:40.244 --> 34:42.494
made your body reject physical touch.

462
34:43.714 --> 34:46.674
It's a defense mechanism caused by your trauma.

463
34:48.154 --> 34:50.844
If you heal from that trauma,

464
34:51.414 --> 34:52.344
your body

465
34:52.994 --> 34:54.833
will slowly stop rejecting physical contact.

466
34:54.834 --> 34:57.424
What if it suddenly stopped rejecting?

467
34:57.994 --> 34:59.424
Can you touch Nadear now?

468
35:01.844 --> 35:03.274
Not Nadear,

469
35:05.274 --> 35:07.404
but a woman I met by accident.

470
35:17.114 --> 35:19.114
When we were close,

471
35:20.804 --> 35:22.484
I didn't feel uncomfortable.

472
35:23.924 --> 35:27.094
I didn't feel awkward like when I was with Nadear...

473
35:27.484 --> 35:29.834
or with any other woman.

474
35:29.984 --> 35:33.584
What did you feel when you were close to her?

475
35:34.374 --> 35:35.564
I wanted to stop,

476
35:37.214 --> 35:38.344
but I couldn't.

477
35:39.374 --> 35:40.854
I couldn't stop myself.

478
35:42.594 --> 35:43.864
Do you like her?

479
35:45.034 --> 35:46.904
I tried not to have any feelings for her.

480
35:47.294 --> 35:48.954
Then what will you do next?

481
35:52.394 --> 35:54.144
What can I do?

482
35:54.884 --> 35:57.323
You know I still have to live with Nadear.

483
35:57.324 --> 35:59.074
But you two already broke up.

484
35:59.214 --> 36:01.374
I can't tell anyone that, Doctor.

485
36:02.094 --> 36:03.504
From an outsider's perspective,

486
36:04.274 --> 36:05.894
we'd still have to be together.

487
36:06.564 --> 36:09.004
I just don't want her to

488
36:09.354 --> 36:11.614
get tangled up in this mess.

489
36:12.574 --> 36:13.964
Let me ask you something.

490
36:14.254 --> 36:16.464
If you could touch Nadear,

491
36:16.714 --> 36:18.094
would anything change?

492
36:22.334 --> 36:23.403
Before we broke up,

493
36:23.404 --> 36:26.784
I already told Nadear that this isn't about physical contact.

494
36:27.494 --> 36:29.414
Even if we'd had sex,

495
36:30.254 --> 36:31.754
we would've broken up anyway.

496
36:33.574 --> 36:35.734
Nadear and I really aren't compatible.

497
36:37.774 --> 36:39.004
Then...

498
36:39.834 --> 36:41.464
why don't you talk to Nadear about this?

499
36:42.254 --> 36:46.094
If that woman can help you feel better,

500
36:46.694 --> 36:48.104
Nadear will understand.

501
36:48.574 --> 36:50.074
And what if she doesn't?

502
36:50.634 --> 36:51.764
I know

503
36:52.354 --> 36:54.104
that you feel bad for Nadear,

504
36:55.894 --> 36:57.824
but I want you to be happy.

505
36:58.454 --> 36:59.814
This is your life.

506
37:00.794 --> 37:03.924
Are you going to let guilt stop you from being happy?

507
37:40.094 --> 37:40.794
Sun.

508
37:42.514 --> 37:42.944
Yes?

509
37:43.434 --> 37:44.134
I'm sorry,

510
37:44.134 --> 37:45.074
I got the wrong person.

511
37:45.754 --> 37:46.894
Oh, okay.

512
38:21.134 --> 38:22.084
Thank you.

513
38:25.414 --> 38:26.734
You broke your promise.

514
38:27.204 --> 38:28.554
Didn't you say you'd run here yesterday?

515
38:29.654 --> 38:30.124
What?

516
38:30.334 --> 38:31.784
Did you run here yesterday?

517
38:32.474 --> 38:34.624
I probably... assumed

518
38:35.374 --> 38:36.414
that we'd meet here.

519
38:38.314 --> 38:39.414
I'm sorry...

520
38:39.684 --> 38:41.414
I had errands yesterday.

521
38:42.444 --> 38:43.224
What if tomorrow...

522
38:43.225 --> 38:44.294
I'm not free tomorrow.

523
38:49.364 --> 38:50.824
But I'm free today.

524
38:52.294 --> 38:53.934
Are you good at gardening?

525
39:00.894 --> 39:02.884
Didn't you say you knew how to grow plants?

526
39:03.194 --> 39:04.634
You said you took care of a rose plant.

527
39:05.394 --> 39:06.873
That was a long time ago,

528
39:06.874 --> 39:08.634
and my father helped me too.

529
39:09.074 --> 39:10.834
If I have to do it alone,

530
39:11.134 --> 39:12.834
I don't know if it'll work out.

531
39:15.894 --> 39:16.934
Then...

532
39:17.964 --> 39:19.514
Let's learn together.

533
39:21.314 --> 39:22.924
Didn't you say you knew how to grow plants?

534
39:25.364 --> 39:27.124
Well, if I said I didn't know how to grow plants,

535
39:27.434 --> 39:28.764
would I get to come with you?

536
39:30.294 --> 39:31.393
You don't have to lie

537
39:31.394 --> 39:33.724
to come with me.

538
39:34.294 --> 39:37.094
You can just say you want to come, and I'll let you come with me.

539
39:44.244 --> 39:45.234
Hello.

540
39:45.644 --> 39:47.254
What plant would you like?

541
39:49.674 --> 39:51.883
I'll get the soil and the rest of the plants

542
39:51.884 --> 39:52.884
for you.

543
39:53.034 --> 39:53.604
Thank you.

544
39:53.604 --> 39:54.604
- Thank you. - Thank you.

545
39:56.564 --> 39:58.504
I thought you only wanted to grow roses,

546
39:58.644 --> 39:59.964
but you wanted to be a cook as well?

547
40:00.884 --> 40:03.944
I've wanted to pick ingredients straight from the garden for a while now.

548
40:04.204 --> 40:05.504
- Mm... - So...

549
40:05.924 --> 40:07.824
Don't you want to grow something as well, Chris?

550
40:09.014 --> 40:11.084
I'm not that into growing plants,

551
40:12.094 --> 40:14.114
but I like the smell of petrichor.

552
40:14.314 --> 40:15.704
It feels refreshing.

553
40:16.044 --> 40:16.934
Then that means...

554
40:17.194 --> 40:18.654
you like the smell of bacteria.

555
40:19.454 --> 40:19.954
Hm?

556
40:22.764 --> 40:24.213
The smell of petrichor

557
40:24.214 --> 40:27.214
comes from plants' natural oils.

558
40:27.444 --> 40:28.874
When it rains,

559
40:29.024 --> 40:31.373
these oils mix with chemicals in the soil,

560
40:31.374 --> 40:33.494
especially geosmin

561
40:34.354 --> 40:35.594
from bacteria,

562
40:36.374 --> 40:38.914
creating the refreshing smell you like.

563
40:39.074 --> 40:41.914
They say this chemical can make you feel calm

564
40:42.234 --> 40:43.794
and relieve stress.

565
40:46.934 --> 40:48.454
You're such a nerd.

566
40:49.354 --> 40:50.834
Do you like nerds, then?

567
41:25.494 --> 41:26.674
Are you alright?

568
41:29.254 --> 41:30.554
We ran through the rain yesterday,

569
41:30.734 --> 41:31.864
and today we ran through the sprinklers.

570
41:32.294 --> 41:33.434
How eventful.

571
41:34.294 --> 41:36.094
But this shouldn't have happened.

572
41:36.334 --> 41:37.573
They could see that we were there,

573
41:37.574 --> 41:39.054
so why did they turn on the sprinklers?

574
41:40.334 --> 41:41.184
I'll talk to them.

575
41:41.814 --> 41:42.684
Chris.

576
41:46.684 --> 41:47.854
Do you smell that?

577
41:51.644 --> 41:52.294
Mm.

578
41:52.994 --> 41:53.774
The smell...

579
41:53.774 --> 41:54.764
of bacteria.

580
41:55.874 --> 41:57.684
It actually helps relieve stress, huh?

581
42:01.814 --> 42:04.044
It's not because of the petrichor, though.

582
42:05.254 --> 42:06.694
Are you saying it's because of me?

583
42:09.174 --> 42:10.814
You're quite a narcissist, huh?

584
42:12.354 --> 42:13.414
Am I wrong, then?

585
42:15.244 --> 42:16.774
If it weren't for you,

586
42:17.694 --> 42:19.934
I would've been so stressed my head would have exploded.

587
42:22.374 --> 42:24.144
I defused the bomb for you,

588
42:24.484 --> 42:26.074
so you don't have to be angry anymore.

589
42:26.974 --> 42:29.084
They probably didn't mean to make their customers wet.

590
42:32.084 --> 42:33.884
How can you be so optimistic?

591
42:36.324 --> 42:38.414
Maybe it's because I've been through terrible things.

592
42:40.094 --> 42:42.734
If I don't look at the bright side,

593
42:43.724 --> 42:46.094
I might not be able to move forward.

594
42:51.574 --> 42:52.894
Let's get our plants.

595
43:00.814 --> 43:04.294
[Third Person]

596
43:06.065 --> 43:09.345
[Third Person]

597
43:12.205 --> 43:13.534
Take a shower right away

598
43:13.535 --> 43:14.655
before you get sick.

599
43:16.735 --> 43:17.615
It's funny

600
43:17.616 --> 43:19.435
how we got wet on different days.

601
43:20.145 --> 43:22.795
But it won't be funny if you get sick.

602
43:23.285 --> 43:24.645
I won't be.

603
43:27.255 --> 43:28.215
I'll take a shower now.

604
43:36.045 --> 43:36.755
Hey!

605
43:37.815 --> 43:39.025
What're you doing?

606
43:41.335 --> 43:43.375
Didn't you tell me to take a shower right away?

607
43:44.245 --> 43:46.375
Well, you don't have to rush that much.

608
43:53.975 --> 43:55.485
You have to survive

609
43:55.825 --> 43:57.145
so we can be together for a long time.

610
44:00.055 --> 44:02.365
I want to see beautiful roses from you too.

611
44:20.015 --> 44:21.164
If you're done unwrapping,

612
44:21.165 --> 44:22.675
you can put it there.

613
44:28.025 --> 44:28.645
Oh!

614
44:29.825 --> 44:30.585
Hey,

615
44:30.586 --> 44:31.625
get back inside.

616
44:39.025 --> 44:40.345
What is it, Chris?

617
44:45.975 --> 44:47.985
Someone might take photos of you.

618
44:48.185 --> 44:50.205
Phone cameras have such powerful zoom nowadays.

619
44:53.885 --> 44:55.485
Just say you're worried about me.

620
44:56.175 --> 44:58.065
No need to explain this much.

621
45:10.805 --> 45:12.305
Don't worry anymore.

622
45:16.295 --> 45:17.935
No one can see me in this room

623
45:19.025 --> 45:20.575
except the one I want them to.

624
45:25.245 --> 45:26.815
I'll have to save the plants.

625
45:41.585 --> 45:42.335
Chris.

626
45:43.245 --> 45:43.975
Oh!

627
45:45.775 --> 45:47.525
You've been out here for a while now.

628
45:47.885 --> 45:49.345
Is there something on your mind?

629
45:49.785 --> 45:51.035
Should we head back inside?

630
45:51.685 --> 45:52.864
I'm fine outside.

631
45:52.865 --> 45:54.585
I like looking at the plants.

632
45:56.805 --> 45:57.835
Is that so?

633
45:58.935 --> 45:59.905
Yeah.

634
46:04.895 --> 46:06.355
Then let me introduce you to them.

635
46:07.005 --> 46:08.595
This is Ri.

636
46:09.065 --> 46:10.594
If it sprouts more leaves,

637
46:10.595 --> 46:12.865
I'll promote it to Ri-ri.

638
46:14.225 --> 46:15.335
And this is...

639
46:15.765 --> 46:16.605
Li.

640
46:17.865 --> 46:20.335
If it grows a bit more, I'll promote it too.

641
46:23.985 --> 46:25.155
Promote it to Li-li?

642
46:25.925 --> 46:26.995
Yeah.

643
46:29.025 --> 46:30.625
And these are...

644
46:31.655 --> 46:33.045
Oo-oo-oo.

645
46:35.365 --> 46:36.715
Oo-oo-oo?

646
46:38.865 --> 46:39.715
Yeah.

647
46:39.985 --> 46:41.465
That's a cute name.

648
46:57.685 --> 46:58.734
Make yourself at home.

649
46:58.735 --> 46:59.975
I'll wait inside.

650
47:09.595 --> 47:11.595
[Nadear]

651
47:25.505 --> 47:26.705
Jeen...

652
47:29.055 --> 47:31.325
Chris has never been like this before.

653
47:33.425 --> 47:35.845
I don't know what to do anymore.

654
47:36.765 --> 47:37.905
What happened, Nadear?

655
47:39.965 --> 47:42.845
I feel like I'm about to lose her.

656
47:45.055 --> 47:47.235
Can you help me, Jeen?

657
47:48.425 --> 47:50.695
I can't lose her.

658
47:51.095 --> 47:54.395
I want Chris to love me like she used to.

659
49:31.125 --> 49:32.615
Are you a dancer?

660
49:35.345 --> 49:36.975
Is that an insult?

661
49:37.865 --> 49:39.045
No.

662
49:39.425 --> 49:40.005
Well...

663
49:40.006 --> 49:41.865
You seem to enjoy music.

664
49:43.185 --> 49:44.615
Are you a DJ?

665
49:46.125 --> 49:46.745
Wrong.

666
49:47.625 --> 49:48.785
Then...

667
49:49.045 --> 49:49.815
a model?

668
49:54.215 --> 49:55.495
Try again.

669
49:56.055 --> 49:57.895
You know what my job is.

670
50:04.225 --> 50:05.355
Are you a doctor?

671
50:06.765 --> 50:07.815
You're smart.

672
50:09.015 --> 50:10.345
No, you are.

673
50:12.425 --> 50:14.944
I don't really work as a doctor much anymore.

674
50:14.945 --> 50:16.745
I'm more on the management side now.

675
50:17.545 --> 50:19.595
I co-own a clinic with my friend.

676
50:21.345 --> 50:22.425
Then...

677
50:22.975 --> 50:25.524
can you look at my face for me, Doc?

678
50:25.525 --> 50:27.375
Are there any adjustments needed?

679
50:40.135 --> 50:41.705
You're already pretty.

680
50:42.785 --> 50:44.255
Your skin is glowing.

681
50:46.815 --> 50:49.015
Your features are well-balanced.

682
50:51.695 --> 50:53.605
Your under-eyes are full and plump.

683
50:55.105 --> 50:56.815
No need for fillers.

684
50:58.175 --> 50:59.585
Your chin...

685
50:59.775 --> 51:01.385
is naturally beautiful.

686
51:03.735 --> 51:05.345
As for your lips...

687
51:07.085 --> 51:08.015
very kissable.

688
51:31.415 --> 51:33.365
It's alright if you can't hug me.

689
51:34.345 --> 51:37.345
I just want you to stay by my side.

690
51:42.805 --> 51:43.585
What's wrong?

691
51:49.465 --> 51:51.335
I was in a car accident several years ago.

692
51:54.935 --> 51:56.145
Does it still hurt?

693
52:03.405 --> 52:06.525
My doctor said the accident made me reject physical contact.

694
52:08.325 --> 52:11.205
It's a defense mechanism in response to trauma.

695
52:14.415 --> 52:15.685
The trauma here?

696
52:22.815 --> 52:25.555
I thought physical touch could help you recover.

697
53:11.925 --> 53:14.895
I don't want you to be in this terrible relationship.

698
53:15.025 --> 53:16.995
Follow your heart, Chris.

699
53:17.365 --> 53:19.755
You make the person you're with feel seen.

700
53:19.935 --> 53:20.915
That's the reason

701
53:21.085 --> 53:22.865
I want to be your friend.

702
53:24.215 --> 53:25.495
Who gave you this?

703
53:26.615 --> 53:27.395
A friend.

704
53:27.985 --> 53:29.614
I don't want to see you in pain

705
53:29.615 --> 53:31.615
or see you sad anymore,

706
53:32.405 --> 53:34.335
because I love you!

707
53:34.625 --> 53:36.095
Am I wrong for that?

708
53:38.425 --> 53:40.235
Friends don't kiss, do they?

709
53:55.215 --> 54:05.184
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

710
54:05.185 --> 54:10.344
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

711
54:10.345 --> 54:14.614
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

712
54:14.615 --> 54:20.334
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

713
54:20.335 --> 54:29.905
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

714
54:29.925 --> 54:35.224
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

715
54:35.225 --> 54:39.534
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

716
54:39.535 --> 54:48.365
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

717
54:48.895 --> 54:57.885
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫
